// sep16a ryouko fuzz divergence_000000 (2026-09-17), minimized. The
// handler-ful `?` under the never arm raises an error built from `n`, a
// let whose init fire no selected arm had read: at x = 2 the interp's
// select tracker re-delivers that fire and the raise lands (n becomes
// 1); the kernel read `n` standing (stale), so the error was not
// deliverable and the handler never ran. A handler-ful `?` under a
// select arm now node-walks whatever its error derives from.
// Expected (both engines): 1 at x = 3.
{let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2, i64:3]); let n = i64:0; {catch(e) n <- e ~ n + i64:1; select x {i64:2 => never(error(`E(n))?), _ => x}}; select x {i64:3 => n, _ => i64:0}}
